*Resolved 2026-10-01*: all 9 =airflow-*= copies were deleted (=bisos/asc=
commit =addaad4=). The planted CBM leaf points at the package CBS by
absolute path. No root-era units were ever re-materialized. See
=bisos-pip/airflow= archived TODO 4.3.

- *What*: =/bisos/asc/web/bin/= holds 8 =airflow-*.pcs= files --- the
  predecessor installation, from before =bisos.airflow= existed as a
  package. They come *first* on PATH:

  #+begin_example
  airflow-webserver-sysd.pcs  -> /bisos/asc/web/bin/airflow-webserver-sysd.pcs
  airflow-sbom.pcs            -> /bisos/asc/web/bin/airflow-sbom.pcs
  airflow-cbs.pcs             -> /bisos/asc/web/bin/airflow-cbs.pcs
  #+end_example

- *Why it matters*: those copies =diff= as pre-migration --- zero
  occurrences of =User=airflow= or =airflowAcctEnvSetup=. Invoking any of
  them *by bare name* re-materializes the **root-era** units over the top of
  the migrated installation, silently and apparently successfully.
- *Why nothing broke*: every invocation during the migration used an
  explicit repo path. Deliberate, but not a durable safeguard.
- *Action*: retire the =/bisos/asc/web/bin/= airflow copies, or ensure the
  package wins on PATH.


