*Resolved 2026-10-01*: =README.org=, =serverSetup= and =AI-DevStatus.org=
were corrected. =AI-Usage.org= was replaced by the =airflowUsage= Blee
panel. The aspirational panels are marked as such. See =bisos-pip/airflow=
archived TODOs 4.1, 4.7 and 4.8 (commit =c40e9bf=).

All still describe the root-based installation:

- =README.org= --- the "4 systemd Units and DB Init" section.
- =py3/panels/bisos.airflow/serverSetup/_nodeBase_/fullUsagePanel-en.org=.
- =AI-Usage.org= --- describes the unit templates with no mention of
  =User=airflow= or =EnvironmentFile=. *Also still untracked in git* (=??=);
  never committed.
- =AI-DevStatus.org= --- still template placeholders for Architecture, What
  Works, What Is Untested, Key Design Decisions.

Pre-existing and separate: most Blee-panel content beyond =serverSetup=
(Postgres maintenance, monitoring/alerting, multi-user management, a
=dynamic_remote_orchestrator= DAG) describes scope that does not exist in
code. Do not cite those panels as evidence of implemented behaviour.


