*Resolved 2026-10-01*: the leaf
=/bisos/platform/sys/cbm/collective/hereWeb/airflow/= exists again in
=bro_rawBisos= (commits =a102cb7=, =11c6fec=). Its =cbmProc.spcs= is now a
real executable, matching =nginx='s, not a symlink. It sets
=cbsSpec="/bisos/git/bxRepos/bisos-pip/airflow/py3/bin/airflow-cbs.pcs"=
and has =cbmProc.control= / =cbmProc.status= beside it.

The leaf =/bisos/platform/sys/cbm/collective/hereWeb/airflow/= (containing
=cbmProc.spcs= -> =cbmProc-airflow.spcs=, plus =.control= and =.status=) was
moved aside and never recreated. =cbs_materialize= does not need it --- its
body is =cbs_sbom= -> =cbs_assemble= -> =sysdUnitsProc ensure all= --- but
CBM-level verbs (=cbm_status=, =cbm_enable=, ...) do.

Asymmetry noticed while investigating: =nginx='s leaf has =cbmProc.spcs= as
a *real 524-byte executable*, whereas airflow's was a *symlink* into the
repo. Airflow's leaf may have been made by hand, which would explain why no
CBS-level command recreates it.


